{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.5266 accuracy, a clear +4.2% gain over the RNA-only baseline (config_001, 0.4849), confirming that adding image features via concat fusion is beneficial. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether multiprofile (with an aggregation step) adds further value on top of the multimodal gain, or whether singleprofile is already sufficient. Question: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) isolates the multiprofile dimension while keeping the proven multimodal+resnet50+concat backbone. Why best next: It is the most informative single experiment because a positive result opens the entire multiprofile+aggregation subspace (transformer aggregation, other encoders) for further exploitation, while a negative result confirms singleprofile sufficiency and redirects budget toward RNA/image encoder or fusion-strategy variations. It directly extends the strongest configuration with one new variable, maximizing information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

